WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.933 --> 00:00:03.202
(honking)

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.371
(purrs)

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.474
(trumpets)

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:13.379 line:0%
AMANDA: Hello, girls.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.648
I have snacks for you.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.083
Come here.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.386 align:start position:0%
The Wallaroo section of the zoo
is Australian themed,

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:23.122 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
but you do not need
an Australian accent to go in.

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:26.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a lot of playgrounds
for the kids to play on.

00:00:26.058 --> 00:00:27.292
There's a water park.

00:00:27.292 --> 00:00:29.729
We have wallabies and koalas.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.932 align:start size:88% position:13%
I would say my favorite
is wallabies.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.667
Hello, Lovebug.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:84% position:16%
You want to come over
for a peanut?

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.238
Good job.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.006 align:start size:88% position:13%
They really like to use
their hands;

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.409 align:start size:91% position:9%
they're super inquisitive
and friendly.

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:44.477
Good job, lady.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:45.745
She's like, bye.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.647
(laughs)

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:50.984 align:start size:88% position:13%
Also in Wallaroo we have
two adult koalas.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:54.120
It is relatively rare
to have koalas in zoos

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.454
in the United States.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.090
ANGELA: Came to see Heathcliff.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
AMANDA: We have Heathcliff,
who is the male koala.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.428 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
He is pretty laid back,
super chilled.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.263 align:start size:81% position:19%
ANGELA: You want
some of this, buddy?

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:06.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
AMANDA: (laughs) He's like,
just put it in there,

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:07.901
we'll see what happens.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.369 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
And then we have Ceduna
who is the female.

00:01:10.369 --> 00:01:12.071 line:0%
She's a little spunkier.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.006 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
ANGELA: Ceduna doing
yoga poses today?

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:16.709 align:start size:91% position:9%
AMANDA: She is. She's been
doing some silly stuff.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.244
(laughs)

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:21.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
Oh, my gosh,
we brought you snacks.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.683 align:start position:0%
KATIE: That's like me
in front of a bowl of ice cream.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.852
AMANDA: Oh, yes. (laughs)

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:28.021
We have not seen
a ton of interest

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.891 align:start size:97% position:3%
between Heathcliff and Ceduna
as far as breeding goes.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.393 align:start position:0%
She seems to be very protective
of her pouch today,

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:35.461
so I'm not sure what's going on.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.363
ANGELA: Oh, really? OK.

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:40.066
Ceduna wears the pants
in that relationship.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.701 align:start size:81% position:19%
They have two
different bedrooms;

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.103 align:start size:81% position:19%
she is welcome to go
to his room,

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:47.574
but Heathcliff goes to her room,
and she'll usually move him out.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.975
So what's going on?

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:50.576 align:start size:81% position:19%
KATIE: She's just
kind of hanging out.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:53.779 align:start size:91% position:9%
ANGELA: We could try to do
a pouch check now.

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:56.449 align:start size:81% position:19%
We do a pouch check
every 30 days,

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.718 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
just to make sure that there's
not a joey in the pouch,

00:01:58.718 --> 00:01:59.919 line:0%
looks OK.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.387 align:start size:97% position:3%
KATIE: I mean,
she's looking pretty relaxed.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.156
So I think if we want
to give it a shot.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.724 align:start position:0%
ANGELA: I think I could probably
stick my finger

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.125
in there now, but...

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.326
KATIE: Give it a shot.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:09.128
(laughs)

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:12.065
ANGELA: No, I don't think so.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.533 align:start size:81% position:19%
Nope, she doesn't
want me touching it.

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:16.970 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
KATIE: Lately, when we
kind of touch near that area,

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.505 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
she's a little bit sensitive;
she'll draw back,

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:22.674
where normally she would be
completely fine with it.

00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:25.812 align:start size:88% position:13%
ANGELA: We might wait
until Monday to do this.

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:26.912
KATIE: OK.

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.382
ANGELA: Just so that
she's not stressed out.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.184 align:start size:91% position:9%
KATIE: She is due
for her two-year checkup.

00:02:32.184 --> 00:02:33.419
ANGELA: My fingers are crossed.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really, really,
really hope we have a joey.

00:02:35.687 --> 00:02:37.690 align:start size:91% position:9%
You know, it just doesn't
seem like we do,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.826
from looking at her
from the outside,

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.860
but it's very possible
that it's at an angle

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it's tucked to the side
and we just don't know.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:47.767 align:start size:97% position:3%
KATIE: Knowing if a koala
is pregnant can be difficult,

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.235
because when they're born

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:53.005
they're only 30 days old
and they're super tiny,

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:56.942
and they crawl into the pouch
and attach to one of the teats.

00:02:56.942 --> 00:03:00.113
When they're that small and
inside kind of a cushy pouch,

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.914
you can't tell.

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.349 align:start size:88% position:13%
ANGELA: We'll just wait
to see what we see

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.151
in the pouch on Monday.

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.318
KATIE: Cross our fingers.

00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:08.754 align:start size:91% position:9%
ANGELA: Alright.
Koalas aren't endangered.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:12.925
However, it's always good
to be on top of genetics,

00:03:12.925 --> 00:03:16.295
so we'd like to keep
that number growing.

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:19.431 align:start size:91% position:9%
But the big picture is not
about the zoo's family,

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:22.868 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's about the potential
of that species

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:25.705 align:start size:81% position:19%
living on for
generations to come.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.540
KATIE: Bye, Ceduna.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.676
You be a good girl.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.177
I'm really excited.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.545
(laughs)

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.851
ALEX: Welcome to Zoo Tampa.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.285
My name is Alex.

00:03:40.285 --> 00:03:41.554
And off to the right-hand side

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:44.023 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're gonna see
the Aldabra tortoises.

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.624 align:start size:84% position:16%
When fully grown,
they can reach weights

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:49.795 align:start size:84% position:16%
of up to and around
500 pounds on average.

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:52.898 align:start position:0%
JASON: Alright, we need a length
and width on this shell here.

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:54.233 line:0%
SPENCER: OK.

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:55.735 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
JASON: Bruce is
an Aldabra tortoise,

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.569 line:0%
which comes from
the Aldabra Atoll

00:03:57.569 --> 00:03:59.805 line:0%
off the east coast of Africa.

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:01.974
SPENCER: 41 and three-fourths.

00:04:01.974 --> 00:04:04.110
JASON: They are the second
largest tortoise species

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.444
in the world.

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:08.614
Brice is actually 57 years old,

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:11.383 align:start size:91% position:9%
but currently there's one
that's about 187

00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.318 align:start size:91% position:9%
that's living on an island
in the Atlantic.

00:04:13.318 --> 00:04:17.990
So he could potentially live
another hundred years or more.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:20.226
You got to get that sweet spot.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:22.228
SPENCER: You can feel
the weight difference.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:26.599
JASON: Yeah, I've noticed that
over the last few weeks, too.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.167 align:start size:84% position:16%
What's concerning
about Bruce this year

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.570 align:start size:91% position:9%
is we've started to notice
weight loss

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:34.273
as well as Bruce isn't
moving around as much.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:36.909
Every winter he does tend
to lose a little weight,

00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:38.944 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he does seem to go
into shutdown mode,

00:04:38.944 --> 00:04:40.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
but this year we kind of saw
a little bit more

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.648
than we're used to.

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:45.651
So we're just concerned
that more is going on.

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.487 align:start size:97% position:3%
We want to make sure we bring
him back to full health

00:04:48.487 --> 00:04:51.157
so he can live with us
for a very long time.

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.325
DR. NICO: OK. Hello.

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:54.526
JASON: Hey, Nico.

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:55.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. NICO: Here we have
Mister Bruce?

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:56.929
JASON: Yep.

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's been eating pretty well
for us, but it's not...

00:04:59.364 --> 00:05:00.466
SPENCER: It's not
where we want it.

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:02.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
JASON: Not where
it's been in the past.

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:03.702
DR. NICO: Bruce is amazing.

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:05.371
He is really cool.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.039 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
Some of them have
different personalities;

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:10.376 align:start position:0% line:0%
some of them are more shy,
but Bruce is a really nice guy.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.111 align:start size:88% position:13%
I just want to make sure
that he is OK.

00:05:13.111 --> 00:05:15.514
I'm hoping that his heart is OK,

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:20.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
so the plan is to get
an electrocardiogram on him.

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.555 align:start size:88% position:13%
If we can have some food
that we can offer him

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:25.357 align:start size:88% position:13%
while we're doing this,
that will be great.

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:28.260
SPENCER: Alright.
DR. NICO: Alright.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.429
JASON: I got him these flowers.

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:31.730
Here you go, buddy.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.532
I won't even give
my wife flowers.

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:35.935
(laughter)

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:39.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. NICO: This instrument is
an electrocardiogram,

00:05:39.304 --> 00:05:40.939
and it gives more information

00:05:40.939 --> 00:05:44.410
about the electrical
activity of the heart.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:46.479 align:start size:88% position:13%
It will probably give us
a really good idea

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:49.381
of what his heart
might be doing.

00:05:49.381 --> 00:05:52.318
SPENCER: It's so hard working
under a 300-pound tortoise.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:53.452
(laughs)

00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:54.887 align:start size:84% position:16%
JASON: This year
we're also seeing him

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.723 align:start size:91% position:9%
have a more difficult time
supporting his body.

00:05:57.723 --> 00:06:02.628
We're worried that we're on
kind of a slope downhill.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:07.200 align:start position:0%
DR. NICO: Ryan, I'm not getting
the reading that I want.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.500
I think the machine
is having trouble,

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.569
'cause his heart rate is so low.

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:14.239
(beeping)

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:16.275
JASON: He's officially a rock.

00:06:18.477 --> 00:06:20.045
DR. NICO: That's it. That's one.

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:22.715 align:start size:91% position:9%
We got a good,
we got a good one in here.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.049
RYAN: OK.

00:06:24.049 --> 00:06:26.519 align:start position:0%
DR. NICO: I think it's
a challenge for any veterinarian

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:28.354 align:start size:84% position:16%
that deals with
this kind of species;

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:31.524 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause he's not a dog,
he's not a cat,

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:33.893
there's not all this
research out there

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:35.828
that we can understand.

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:39.598
Oh, let's just try Mr. Al.
I would love to have Al.

00:06:39.598 --> 00:06:41.366
JASON: We're gonna go and do Al.

00:06:41.366 --> 00:06:42.768
We want to get a good baseline

00:06:42.768 --> 00:06:46.839
of what a healthy tortoise
would have for a heart rate,

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:49.074 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
and we can then compare that
to Bruce's

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:50.876 line:0%
to indicate if there's problems.

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:52.578 line:0%
(beeping)

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:55.247
DR. NICO: I think that's
probably right then, Ryan.

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:56.281
'Cause I'm getting...

00:06:56.281 --> 00:06:57.350
RYAN: About 12 beats per minute?

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.751
DR. NICO: Yes.

00:06:58.751 --> 00:07:05.124 align:start size:97% position:3%
So we're getting a more normal
beating on Mr. Al here.

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:08.327
Bruce was a lot slower.

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:10.329 align:start size:81% position:19%
There might be
something going on.

00:07:10.329 --> 00:07:12.131 align:start position:0%
What I want to make sure is
that you guys keep feeding him,

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.265
feeding him, feeding him,

00:07:13.265 --> 00:07:16.369 align:start size:84% position:16%
and report of any kind
of little change.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.704 align:start position:0%
JASON: Hopefully it's not
something major with his heart,

00:07:18.704 --> 00:07:20.039
because that's something

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:22.475
that we'll have a really
difficult time rectifying

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:25.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I don't want to say bye
to Bruce anytime soon.

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:33.452
(squeaking)

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:35.054
(growl)

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.828 align:start size:81% position:19%
JACKIE: Who wouldn't
love that face?

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:44.696
Look how cute he is.

00:07:44.696 --> 00:07:47.666 line:0%
Mentari is a Sulawesi babirusa.

00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:52.337 line:0%
Babirusa literally translates
to "pig deer" in Indonesian.

00:07:52.337 --> 00:07:56.475 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
I love Mentari, I really do,
with all my heart.

00:07:56.475 --> 00:07:58.877
He could do this all day long.

00:07:58.877 --> 00:08:01.246
I've raised Mentari
since he was a baby.

00:08:01.246 --> 00:08:04.883
Oh, he was about this, this big.

00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:06.786 align:start size:88% position:13%
He's coming up to be
about two years old now,

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.888 align:start size:97% position:3%
and reaching sexual maturity,
so that means

00:08:08.888 --> 00:08:11.056
we're gonna need to start
finding him a girlfriend

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:14.226 align:start size:97% position:3%
and increase the population
of babirusas around the world.

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:16.295
The female that Mentari
is getting paired with

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:19.732 align:start position:0%
is actually at another facility,
so sometime soon

00:08:19.732 --> 00:08:21.666
we're gonna actually have
to say goodbye to him.

00:08:21.666 --> 00:08:24.136 align:start size:84% position:16%
Why are you fascinated
with my ring today?

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:25.337
(laughs)

00:08:25.337 --> 00:08:27.406 align:start size:97% position:3%
But we do have two weeks left
with Mentari,

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:28.574
where I'll get to spoil him

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:30.309
before he actually
gets transferred

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:32.745 align:start size:88% position:13%
and hopefully start
a new family of his own.

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:35.481 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's definitely gonna be
bittersweet to see him leave.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.682
I don't have any food
for you right now.

00:08:37.682 --> 00:08:39.084
Before he goes, he is scheduled

00:08:39.084 --> 00:08:40.786 align:start size:81% position:19%
for a full exam
at the vet's office,

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.855 align:start size:88% position:13%
which includes
trimming his tusks back.

00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:45.524 align:start size:97% position:3%
In the wild, there's actually
been cases shown

00:08:45.524 --> 00:08:47.526
where the male babirusa's tusks

00:08:47.526 --> 00:08:51.196 align:start size:91% position:9%
grow back into their skull
and kill them.

00:08:51.196 --> 00:08:53.999 align:start size:91% position:9%
Alright.
Almost ready, little man.

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:56.368 align:start position:0%
In order to get Mentari
to hold still for the tusk trim,

00:08:56.368 --> 00:08:58.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're gonna have to give him
a sedation.

00:08:58.371 --> 00:09:00.138
You're alright, sir.

00:09:00.138 --> 00:09:02.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today we are gonna be doing
a mock session

00:09:02.407 --> 00:09:05.911
of a hip inject with Mentari.

00:09:05.911 --> 00:09:07.747
You want to get some scratches?

00:09:07.747 --> 00:09:10.282 align:start position:0%
Katie, do you want to try
scratching him with that brush?

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:12.684 line:0%
KATIE: Mentari loves a rubdown.

00:09:12.684 --> 00:09:14.853
JACKIE: Oh, what is that, sir?

00:09:14.853 --> 00:09:16.555
There we go.

00:09:16.555 --> 00:09:17.590
KATIE: Oh, yeah.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.191
JACKIE: Good job, Mister.

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:20.959 align:start size:81% position:19%
