the most compassionate thing

00:37:15.366 --> 00:37:17.134
that can happen,

00:37:17.134 --> 00:37:20.471 align:start size:91% position:9%
and I definitely think
that's the case for Bruce.

00:37:20.471 --> 00:37:22.540 align:start size:88% position:13%
JASON: He was an amazing
ambassador.

00:37:22.540 --> 00:37:24.041
He touched a lot of lives.

00:37:24.041 --> 00:37:26.310
He, he was a great tortoise

00:37:26.310 --> 00:37:28.245
even when he didn't
want to cooperate.

00:37:28.245 --> 00:37:29.480
(laughs)

00:37:29.480 --> 00:37:32.082
Yeah, I will miss Bruce.

00:37:32.082 --> 00:37:34.218
We'll all miss Bruce.

00:37:39.490 --> 00:37:41.291
(trumpets)

00:37:41.291 --> 00:37:47.431
♪ ♪

00:37:47.431 --> 00:37:48.566
TIFFANY: Look at Dira.

00:37:48.566 --> 00:37:50.000
DEVON: Oh, my gosh.

00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:51.935
TIFFANY: How many times a day
do we say, "Look at Dira?"

00:37:51.935 --> 00:37:53.838
DEVON: Oh, one million. (laughs)

00:37:53.838 --> 00:37:55.973 align:start size:84% position:16%
TIFFANY: Oh, my gosh,
you're so cute.

00:37:55.973 --> 00:37:58.241
SUSAN: You're so cute.

00:37:58.241 --> 00:38:00.111
KAELA: Hello.
AMANDA: Hi.

00:38:00.111 --> 00:38:02.145 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
AMANDA: So Ceduna's joey
has started

00:38:02.145 --> 00:38:04.047 line:0%
to emerge more from the pouch.

00:38:04.047 --> 00:38:05.816 line:0%
KAELA: Can we see its face?

00:38:05.816 --> 00:38:08.519
AMANDA: We want
to see your baby.

00:38:08.519 --> 00:38:09.853
KAELA: It's moving.

00:38:09.853 --> 00:38:12.155 align:start position:0%
AMANDA: The gestation for koalas
is only 30 days

00:38:12.155 --> 00:38:14.091
before the baby comes out
and moves into the pouch,

00:38:14.091 --> 00:38:16.160
so it's extremely
underdeveloped.

00:38:16.160 --> 00:38:18.929 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
And then it stays in there
for close to six months

00:38:18.929 --> 00:38:20.664
before it starts venturing out.

00:38:20.664 --> 00:38:24.769 align:start size:81% position:19%
We're probably at
the 170-ish day mark

00:38:24.769 --> 00:38:26.903 align:start size:88% position:13%
based on the development
we've seen.

00:38:26.903 --> 00:38:29.106
So we should be seeing
more and more of it.

00:38:29.106 --> 00:38:30.408
Uncross your leg.

00:38:30.408 --> 00:38:33.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
KAELA: I know. Put that leg,
straddle that pole.

00:38:33.444 --> 00:38:35.846 align:start size:81% position:19%
AMANDA: Can you like
just do this?

00:38:35.846 --> 00:38:36.847
KAELA: Lay like this.

00:38:36.847 --> 00:38:38.348
AMANDA: Can you move?

00:38:38.348 --> 00:38:41.384
(laughs)

00:38:41.384 --> 00:38:45.055
KAELA: Ugh, you're
giving us nothing.

00:38:45.055 --> 00:38:46.724 align:start size:88% position:13%
Ceduna is being
one stubborn mom today,

00:38:46.724 --> 00:38:48.926
so we are gonna see if
we can maybe, just maybe,

00:38:48.926 --> 00:38:50.928 align:start size:97% position:3%
bribe her with some delicious
eucalyptus branches

00:38:50.928 --> 00:38:53.797
to show us her joey.

00:38:53.797 --> 00:38:55.266
Alright.

00:38:57.401 --> 00:39:00.070
Want some more food?

00:39:00.070 --> 00:39:01.572
You hungry?

00:39:01.572 --> 00:39:05.543
♪ ♪

00:39:05.543 --> 00:39:07.611
Is that an eye?

00:39:07.611 --> 00:39:08.679
(gasps)

00:39:15.385 --> 00:39:16.821 line:0%
KAELA: Is than an eye?

00:39:16.821 --> 00:39:21.157 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
(gasps) I see its face!
Look at that little cute nose!

00:39:21.157 --> 00:39:24.195
We've just been waiting
and waiting patiently,

00:39:24.195 --> 00:39:25.228
or impatiently.

00:39:25.228 --> 00:39:26.363
(laughs)

00:39:26.363 --> 00:39:28.198
Oh, it's so cute.

00:39:28.198 --> 00:39:31.167 align:start size:91% position:9%
We see a little face
peeking out, a little eye.

00:39:31.167 --> 00:39:33.837
It looks bright-eyed and very
healthy, so we're very excited.

00:39:33.837 --> 00:39:36.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's our first time getting
to see a little joey.

00:39:36.640 --> 00:39:39.142
Looks just like Ceduna.

00:39:39.142 --> 00:39:41.244
Like a little miniature koala.

00:39:41.244 --> 00:39:43.180
AMANDA: We're assuming
it's maybe that big.

00:39:43.180 --> 00:39:45.549 align:start size:81% position:19%
It looks like
it might have a head

00:39:45.549 --> 00:39:47.418
like the size of a squirrel.

00:39:47.418 --> 00:39:49.686 align:start size:97% position:3%
KAELA: Eventually it'll start
riding on mom's back

00:39:49.686 --> 00:39:51.355 align:start size:84% position:16%
and will start eating
the eucalyptus

00:39:51.355 --> 00:39:55.092 align:start size:91% position:9%
and we'll get to see more
and watch it grow up.

00:39:55.092 --> 00:40:00.831
♪ ♪

00:40:00.831 --> 00:40:07.204
♪ ♪

00:40:07.204 --> 00:40:10.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
KATIE: Good morning.
You ready for your checkup?

00:40:10.608 --> 00:40:12.675 align:start position:0%
DR. LAUREN: Today we're gonna go
check up on Stuart.

00:40:12.675 --> 00:40:14.545
He's our male southern stingray.

00:40:14.545 --> 00:40:16.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
His coloration was off,
he looked yellow,

00:40:16.347 --> 00:40:19.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
he had a really nasty, thick
mucus layer on him,

00:40:19.116 --> 00:40:21.184
and he had lost some weight.

00:40:21.184 --> 00:40:23.520 align:start position:0%
KATIE: Stuart's actually right,
ready to go.

00:40:23.520 --> 00:40:24.955
DR. LAUREN: OK, perfect.

00:40:24.955 --> 00:40:26.389
We'll bring him up over here,
we'll get a weight on him,

00:40:26.389 --> 00:40:28.858 align:start size:91% position:9%
and I'll just do
a quick look on his skin.

00:40:28.858 --> 00:40:31.962 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
Stuart has been on a couple
of weeks' worth of antibiotics

00:40:31.962 --> 00:40:33.597
so I'm gonna see how he did.

00:40:33.597 --> 00:40:36.466 align:start size:81% position:19%
KATIE: OK, I'm gonna
go behind him.

00:40:36.466 --> 00:40:37.901
Going forward. Ah!

00:40:37.901 --> 00:40:38.902
DR. LAUREN: You got him.

00:40:38.902 --> 00:40:40.204 align:start size:78% position:22%
KATIE: Nope.
DR. LAUREN: Nope.

00:40:40.204 --> 00:40:43.407 align:start size:91% position:9%
KATIE: He slid underneath.
He knows. (laughs)

00:40:43.407 --> 00:40:44.975
Ah.

00:40:44.975 --> 00:40:46.243
Ah, he saw it.

00:40:46.243 --> 00:40:47.744 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. LAUREN: Stingrays are
really fast swimmers

00:40:47.744 --> 00:40:51.281
and Stuart's evading us, which
is actually a really good sign.

00:40:51.281 --> 00:40:53.117
KATIE: I'll try this one.
This one's a lot lighter.

00:40:53.117 --> 00:40:54.251
DR. LAUREN: OK.

00:40:54.251 --> 00:40:56.887
KATIE: OK.

00:40:56.887 --> 00:40:57.988
OK, I'm gonna lift up.

00:40:57.988 --> 00:40:59.623 align:start size:84% position:16%
DR. LAUREN: And scoop.
Perfect, nice job.

00:40:59.623 --> 00:41:01.458
KATIE: There you go.

00:41:01.458 --> 00:41:03.327
DR. LAUREN: Alright.

00:41:03.327 --> 00:41:04.862
His skin is much better.

00:41:04.862 --> 00:41:06.363
He's not as yellow.

00:41:06.363 --> 00:41:09.365
KATIE: No.

00:41:09.365 --> 00:41:10.467
DR. LAUREN: Every stingray will

00:41:10.467 --> 00:41:11.868
have a little bit
of variation there.

00:41:11.868 --> 00:41:14.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what I'm seeing today is
nowhere near what I saw

00:41:14.738 --> 00:41:17.741 align:start size:84% position:16%
on the day when we had
our first concerns.

00:41:17.741 --> 00:41:19.643 align:start position:0%
And all those tracking lesions,
the slime layers,

00:41:19.643 --> 00:41:20.644
I don't see anymore.

00:41:20.644 --> 00:41:21.845
KATIE: Yeah.

00:41:21.845 --> 00:41:24.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
DR. LAUREN: That's awesome,
that's awesome.

00:41:24.148 --> 00:41:26.383 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, I mean, we definitely want
to back up my impression

00:41:26.383 --> 00:41:28.519 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he's looking better,
I want to get a weight on him.

00:41:28.519 --> 00:41:29.686
KATIE: Oh, dear god.

00:41:29.686 --> 00:41:30.987
DR. LAUREN: If Stuart
hasn't gained weight

00:41:30.987 --> 00:41:33.523 align:start size:91% position:9%
then that means we haven't
fixed the issue.

00:41:33.523 --> 00:41:35.559
KATIE: 6.5.

00:41:35.559 --> 00:41:37.260
Oh, god.

00:41:37.260 --> 00:41:39.363
He definitely gained weight.

00:41:39.363 --> 00:41:41.498 align:start size:91% position:9%
DR. LAUREN: So he's gained
a whole kg.

00:41:41.498 --> 00:41:42.733
So that's awesome.

00:41:42.733 --> 00:41:44.501 align:start size:88% position:13%
Super excited,
he's gained a kilogram,

00:41:44.501 --> 00:41:46.503
so a little over two pounds.

00:41:46.503 --> 00:41:48.004 align:start size:78% position:22%
I think he was
immune suppressed,

00:41:48.004 --> 00:41:49.506
and what happens is
that leaves them open

00:41:49.506 --> 00:41:51.007
to secondary infections.

00:41:51.007 --> 00:41:54.545
So I think using antibiotics
was a combination for success.

00:41:54.545 --> 00:41:57.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he looks fantastic.
Really nice job.

00:41:57.214 --> 00:42:00.083 align:start size:81% position:19%
KATIE: I am ecstatic
for the good news

00:42:00.083 --> 00:42:03.754 line:0%
that Stuart is looking so much
better and he's gaining weight.

00:42:03.754 --> 00:42:05.890 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
It's a very good day
for all of us.

00:42:10.494 --> 00:42:13.297
(bellows)

00:42:13.297 --> 00:42:15.999
CHRISTI: Mbali!

00:42:15.999 --> 00:42:18.368
Mbali!

00:42:18.368 --> 00:42:20.437
Come on, pretty girl.

00:42:20.437 --> 00:42:22.773
Let's come inside.

00:42:22.773 --> 00:42:27.444
Let's get inside,
get some breakfast.

00:42:27.444 --> 00:42:29.780
Look at the enthusiasm.

00:42:29.780 --> 00:42:30.980
(laughs)

00:42:30.980 --> 00:42:34.717
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

00:42:34.717 --> 00:42:37.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is it too hot?
You gonna hang in the shade?

00:42:37.487 --> 00:42:40.524
Yeah, I see you peeking.

00:42:40.524 --> 00:42:42.392
(laughs)

00:42:42.392 --> 00:42:45.662 align:start size:88% position:13%
She's really not moving.
I'm talking to a log.

00:42:45.662 --> 00:42:48.165
♪ ♪

00:42:48.165 --> 00:42:52.836
♪ ♪

00:42:52.836 --> 00:42:54.971
AMANDA: Hello.

00:42:54.971 --> 00:42:58.075
Good morning, gorgeous girl.

00:42:58.075 --> 00:43:00.811
We brought you a snack
for you and your baby.

00:43:00.811 --> 00:43:07.283
♪ ♪

00:43:07.283 --> 00:43:08.952
It's so cute now.

00:43:08.952 --> 00:43:11.254
It's like a mini koala.

00:43:11.254 --> 00:43:13.123
His head is so round and furry.

00:43:13.123 --> 00:43:14.124
ANGELA: It's perfect.

00:43:14.124 --> 00:43:15.125
AMANDA: It is perfect.

00:43:15.125 --> 00:43:16.460
(laughs)

00:43:16.460 --> 00:43:17.795
ANGELA: The joey's out.

00:43:17.795 --> 00:43:19.296
Very exciting.

00:43:19.296 --> 00:43:21.465 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
We did find out that
the little joey is a male

00:43:21.465 --> 00:43:25.302 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
and his name is Sydney,
and it's adorable.

00:43:25.302 --> 00:43:26.903
Just in love with this baby.

00:43:26.903 --> 00:43:29.138 align:start size:88% position:13%
AMANDA: (laughs) I know.
I think everyone is.

00:43:29.138 --> 00:43:31.108
ANGELA: Oh, it's just too much.

00:43:31.108 --> 00:43:32.109
It's perfect.

00:43:32.109 --> 00:43:33.343
AMANDA: It is perfect.

00:43:33.343 --> 00:43:34.978 align:start size:84% position:16%
ANGELA: It's a perfect
koala joey.

00:43:34.978 --> 00:43:37.314
AMANDA: Looks a lot like Ceduna.

00:43:37.314 --> 00:43:38.448 align:start size:88% position:13%
ANGELA: Let's come back
later today.

00:43:38.448 --> 00:43:40.751
AMANDA: OK. Twist my arm.

00:43:40.751 --> 00:43:43.920
ANGELA: OK. (laughs)

00:43:43.920 --> 00:43:45.589 align:start size:81% position:19%
We're really excited
about the joey,

00:43:45.589 --> 00:43:48.124 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it's great to grow
our family,

00:43:48.124 --> 00:43:52.129 line:0%
but in a bigger picture, it's
fantastic for conservation.

00:43:52.129 --> 00:43:56.132 line:0%
What we've done on our part
is producing one more koala

00:43:56.132 --> 00:44:00.370 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
to meet that goal
of genetic diversity.

00:44:00.370 --> 00:44:02.939 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
It's incredible.
It feels really good.

00:44:02.939 --> 00:44:06.944 align:start position:0% line:0%
I'm proud to be part of the team
that helped make this happen.

00:44:09.279 --> 00:44:11.181 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
